    "title": "Do not mess with past FTM success",
    "text": "To the editor:\nAs a past town moderator, I believe the traditional Financial Town Meeting format (open discussion followed by motions and voting) has served the town well.\nThe moderator’s job is to ensure all citizens’ right to participate in the annual FTM is protected. I never saw evidence that any citizen was too embarrassed or intimidated to speak their mind.\nOr to vote.\nThe classic Norman Rockwell painting of a New England town meeting presents a civic ideal: a man dressed in work clothes, notes in hand, expresses his position to the assembly of his fellow citizens. A child looks on as the man speaks, absorbing an important lesson in civics.\nThat lesson is taught annually in Jamestown and in all the towns using the open discussion method of adopting a budget.\nJamestown has been blessed with excellent government. The annual Financial Town Meeting has been an important part of that governance.\nCaution is urged when changes are proposed.\nJohn Austin Murphy\nHamilton Avenue",
